      "message": "Let a stranger propose a change, and nobody's runner run it unasked\n\nA sixth verb, propose, strictly smaller than push: it opens a change on\na repository and reaches the changes you opened, to revise, claim and\nabandon them, and nothing else. A public repository gives it to\neveryone signed in when its policy says proposals are open; being on\nthe organisation that owns a repository carries it; a grant gives it to\none person on any repository. A change opened under propose alone is\nrecorded as a proposal, in the event and on the change, and stays one:\nit says what the reviewers were looking at. A proposal counts against\nthe proposer's open changes rather than the owner's, does not attempt\na task, and a push whose Change-Id names somebody else's change is\nrefused rather than joined.\n\nNobody's word lands anything by being said. On a proposal the owner's\nown claim is testimony: it meets the passing-test requirement only once\na runner has reproduced it, or when somebody holding push made the\nclaim. And no runner runs a stranger's command unasked: runners' loops\nleave a proposal out of what they owe until somebody holding merge or\nverify lets them at it, an event of its own, from the change's page or\nthe API. Pre-receive admits a proposer's push and caps what it carries; the\nrepository page tells a proposer what their push will open; the\nchanges list and the change page mark proposals; the MCP gains\nadmit_change and discard_change.\n\nA proposer's room is their own: so many proposals open on one\nrepository, so many a day, so much in one push, three numbers in the\nquota like the rest, with the operator's flags and per-principal\noverrides. And somebody holding merge may discard a proposal: it is\nabandoned with a reason, its refs/changes/N/* leave git, and gc\nreclaims what nothing names; reconciliation leaves a discarded\nproposal's refs gone. Ordinary abandonment keeps every revision, as\nit always did.\n\nTask: t-3rt4dz9pxk66ybjym7mcy909em\nChange-Id: Ipropose0132\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
